  "title": "R: the only unit a trader needs",
  "hook": "You made $500. Proud? Depends what you risked.",
  "takeaway": "R is what you lose if your stop gets hit: (entry − stop) × shares, fixed before you buy. Measure every result with that ruler. A $500 win is +5R on $100 risk and +0.25R on $2,000. Losers should all be −1R; anything bigger means the stop moved or price gapped.",
